<main><nav class="gb-jumps" aria-label="Geralt of Rivia"><a href="#profile">The character</a><a href="#path">The witcher’s path</a><a href="#people">Close companions</a><a href="#games">The games</a></nav><p class="gb-note">The books and the game continuation are labelled separately. The summaries introduce the stories without revealing their endings.</p>
<section id="profile"><div class="gb-intro"><img class="gb-portrait" src="images/portraits/geralt-bio.jpg" alt="Geralt of Rivia"><div><h2>More than a monster hunter</h2><p>A witcher, a monster hunter, and a man who rarely manages to stand aside. His story is about more than contracts and battles: it is about choices, friendship, and family.</p><p>Geralt makes a living by tracking dangerous creatures, lifting curses, and dealing with other people’s troubles. Swords, potions, and signs help him survive, but force cannot solve every problem.</p><p>Behind his restrained manner and sharp replies is a man deeply attached to his friends. His wish to remain neutral repeatedly clashes with the need to protect those he cares about.</p><dl class="gb-facts"><div><dt>Known as</dt><dd>The White Wolf</dd></div><div><dt>School</dt><dd>School of the Wolf</dd></div><div><dt>Profession</dt><dd>Monster hunter</dd></div></dl></div></div></section>
<section id="path"><span class="gb-tag">Book background</span><h2>The witcher’s path</h2><ol class="gb-steps"><li><span class="gb-tag">Kaer Morhen</span><h3>Training and trials</h3><p>Geralt’s childhood is tied to the witcher stronghold. Training, mutations, and harsh discipline prepare him to face creatures that ordinary people cannot.</p></li><li><span class="gb-tag">On the road</span><h3>The cost of neutrality</h3><p>Travelling between towns and villages, Geralt encounters more than monsters. A contract can become a confrontation with fear, prejudice, and human cruelty.</p></li><li><span class="gb-tag">Yennefer and Ciri</span><h3>A family of his own</h3><p>His relationship with Yennefer and his bond with Ciri change his life. Caring for them becomes more important than solitude or staying out of other people’s conflicts.</p></li></ol></section>
<section id="people"><h2>The people closest to him</h2><p>Five relationships that shape Geralt’s story.</p><div class="gb-grid"><article class="gb-card"><span class="gb-tag">Adopted daughter</span><h3>Ciri</h3><p>Destiny connects her to Geralt, but care and trust make them a family. To him, she is far more than a prophecy.</p></article><article class="gb-card"><span class="gb-tag">Love and an equal</span><h3>Yennefer</h3><p>A sorceress from Vengerberg. Their relationship is complicated, and their care for Ciri is one of their strongest bonds.</p></article><article class="gb-card"><span class="gb-tag">Friend and ally</span><h3>Triss Merigold</h3><p>A sorceress close to Geralt and Yennefer. She helps Ciri at Kaer Morhen and has a significant role in the games.</p></article><article class="gb-card"><span class="gb-tag">Friend and storyteller</span><h3>Dandelion</h3><p>A poet and bard who shares Geralt’s travels. His ballads turn the witcher’s adventures into legends.</p></article><article class="gb-card"><span class="gb-tag">Mentor</span><h3>Vesemir</h3><p>An experienced witcher of Kaer Morhen and Geralt’s teacher. He connects Geralt to the stronghold, his school, and his fellow witchers.</p></article></div></section>
<section id="games"><h2>The story continues in the games</h2><p>CD PROJEKT RED’s games present their own continuation of the books. Player choices affect relationships and outcomes.</p><details><summary>Show the three game premises · mild spoilers</summary><div class="gb-games"><article><h3>The Witcher</h3><p>Geralt returns with his memory lost. Looking for answers draws him into conflicts shaped by competing interests.</p></article><article><h3>The Witcher 2: Assassins of Kings</h3><p>The witcher becomes caught in a political crisis. He must investigate the deaths of rulers while trying to recover his past.</p></article><article><h3>The Witcher 3: Wild Hunt</h3><p>The search for Ciri takes Geralt through war-torn lands. Family, old connections, and the threat of the Wild Hunt take centre stage.</p></article></div></details><a class="gb-cta" href="gallery.php">Explore the gallery</a><div class="gb-source">More about the world and characters: <a href="https://www.thewitcher.com/">The Witcher</a> · <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Witcher">The Witcher — books</a></div></section></main><?php endif; ?><footer><p><?= htmlspecialchars($lang['footer_text']) ?></p></footer></body></html>
